    {
      "items": [
        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "from_string": "Default state — desktop layout\n\n1. 3 media items → 3 full-width stacked + View Gallery button\n2. 4 media items → 2 full-width + 2-up grid + View Gallery button\n3. 5 media items → 2 full-width + 2-up grid + View Gallery +1 button\n4. 6 media items → 2 full-width + 4-up grid + View Gallery button\n5. 7+ media items → 2 full-width + 4-up grid + View Gallery +X button (X = total minus 6)\n6. Video items slot into the layout based on their position in the media array and are not treated differently to photo items for layout purposes.\n\nshowGalleryButton prop\n\n7. Given showGalleryButton is false, then no View Gallery button renders regardless of media count.\n8. Given showGalleryButton is true, then the View Gallery button renders per the layout thresholds above and is visible and tappable.\n\nDefault state — mobile\n\n9. Given the component renders on mobile, then all media items display in a swipeable single-image carousel with a dot indicator bar regardless of media count.\n10. Given a shopper swipes, then the active dot indicator updates to reflect the current position.\n11. Given showGalleryButton is true on mobile, then the View Gallery button is visible and tappable.\n\nExpanded state — overlay shell\n\n12. Given the View Gallery button is activated, then the gallery opens full-screen taking over the entire viewport.\n13. Given the gallery is open, then clicking the close icon dismisses the overlay and returns the shopper to their previous scroll position on the PDP.\n\nExpanded state — gallery header (desktop)\n\n14. Given the gallery is open on desktop, then a sticky header is visible at the top of the overlay containing: product name, active colour name, close icon, and model avatar thumbnails.\n15. Given the product has multiple colour variants, then the header includes a colour selector.\n16. Given a shopper clicks a model avatar thumbnail, then the gallery scrolls to the corresponding image set for that model.\n\nExpanded state — gallery header (mobile)\n\n17. Given the gallery is open on mobile, then a sticky header is visible containing: product name, close icon, and colour selector. Model avatar thumbnails are not shown on mobile.\n\nExpanded state — image content\n\n18. Given the gallery is open, then the full media array renders as a vertically scrollable stack of full-width media items.\n19. Given the gallery renders, then images are served in an optimised format at the appropriate resolution per breakpoint.\n\nEmpty & error states\n\n20. Given no media items exist for the product, then the component does not render and no broken layout is shown.\n21. Given an image fails to load, then the surrounding layout is maintained without a broken image rendering.\n\nAccessibility\n\n22. Given the gallery overlay opens, then focus moves into it and is trapped within until closed.\n23. Given the gallery overlay closes, then focus returns to the View Gallery button that triggered it.\n24. The overlay has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n25. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA.\n\nOpen items\n\n@Kiera — the gallery overlay and gallery header are not yet componentized in the Design System Figma (node 3093-81721 in the Designs file). Please extract before dev picks this up.",
          "to_string": "*Default state — desktop layout*\n\n1. 3 media items → 3 full-width stacked + View Gallery button\n2. 4 media items → 2 full-width + 2-up grid + View Gallery button\n3. 5 media items → 2 full-width + 2-up grid + View Gallery +1 button\n4. 6 media items → 2 full-width + 4-up grid + View Gallery button\n5. 7+ media items → 2 full-width + 4-up grid + View Gallery +X button (X = total minus 6)\n6. Video items slot into the layout based on their position in the media array and are not treated differently to photo items for layout purposes.\n\n*showGalleryButton prop*\n\n7. Given showGalleryButton is false, then no View Gallery button renders regardless of media count.\n8. Given showGalleryButton is true, then the View Gallery button renders per the layout thresholds above and is visible and tappable.\n\n*Default state — mobile*\n\n9. Given the component renders on mobile, then all media items display in a swipeable single-image carousel with a dot indicator bar regardless of media count.\n10. Given a shopper swipes, then the active dot indicator updates to reflect the current position.\n11. Given showGalleryButton is true on mobile, then the View Gallery button is visible and tappable.\n\n*Expanded state — overlay shell*\n\n12. Given the View Gallery button is activated, then the gallery opens full-screen taking over the entire viewport.\n13. Given the gallery is open, then clicking the close icon dismisses the overlay and returns the shopper to their previous scroll position on the PDP.\n\n*Expanded state — gallery header (desktop)*\n\n14. Given the gallery is open on desktop, then a sticky header is visible at the top of the overlay containing: product name, active colour name, close icon, and model avatar thumbnails.\n15. Given the product has multiple colour variants, then the header includes a colour selector.\n16. Given a shopper clicks a model avatar thumbnail, then the gallery scrolls to the corresponding image set for that model.\n\n*Expanded state — gallery header (mobile)*\n\n17. Given the gallery is open on mobile, then a sticky header is visible containing: product name, close icon, and colour selector. Model avatar thumbnails are not shown on mobile.\n\n*Expanded state — image content*\n\n18. Given the gallery is open, then the full media array renders as a vertically scrollable stack of full-width media items.\n19. Given the gallery renders, then images are served in an optimised format at the appropriate resolution per breakpoint.\n\n*Empty & error states*\n\n20. Given no media items exist for the product, then the component does not render and no broken layout is shown.\n21. Given an image fails to load, then the surrounding layout is maintained without a broken image rendering.\n\n*Accessibility*\n\n22. Given the gallery overlay opens, then focus moves into it and is trapped within until closed.\n23. Given the gallery overlay closes, then focus returns to the View Gallery button that triggered it.\n24. The overlay has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n25. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA.",
          "from_id": "",
          "to_id": ""
        }
