      "items": [
        {
          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "As a Developer, I want a reusable pdp/carousel React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it can be consumed by pdp/hero to render the product image and video gallery on the PDP.\n\nThe component renders a sequence of media items (photo and video) in a stacked layout on desktop and a swipeable carousel on mobile. The desktop layout adapts based on total media count. Video is treated as a standard media item and slots into the layout based on its position in the product's media array. The component renders a View Gallery button as a trigger only — the gallery overlay is a separate component and out of scope for this story.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n\nDesktop layout — media count thresholds\n\n# 3 media items → 3 full-width stacked + View Gallery button\n# 4 media items → 2 full-width + 2-up grid + View Gallery button\n# 5 media items → 2 full-width + 2-up grid + View Gallery +1 button\n# 6 media items → 2 full-width + 4-up grid + View Gallery button\n# 7+ media items → 2 full-width + 4-up grid + View Gallery +X button (X = total minus 6)\n# Video items slot into the layout based on their position in the media array — they are not treated differently to photo items for layout purposes.\n\nshowGalleryButton prop\n\n# Given showGalleryButton is false, then no View Gallery button renders regardless of media count.\n# Given showGalleryButton is true, then the View Gallery button renders per the layout thresholds above and is visible and tappable — overlay behaviour is out of scope for this story.\n\nMobile\n\n# Given the component renders on mobile, then all media items display in a swipeable single-image carousel with a dot indicator bar regardless of media count.\n# Given a shopper swipes, then the active dot indicator updates to reflect the current position.\n# Given showGalleryButton is true on mobile, then the View Gallery button is visible and tappable.\n\nEmpty & error states\n\n# Given no media items exist for the product, then the component does not render and no broken layout is shown.\n# Given an image fails to load, then the surrounding layout is maintained without a broken image rendering — fallback behaviour TBD, see open items.\n\nAccessibility\n\n# The carousel is fully keyboard navigable and meets WCAG 2.1 AA.\n\nOpen Items:\n\n@Kiera — please confirm media count threshold logic is correct per design specs shared.\n\n@Kiera — please confirm fallback behaviour when an image fails to load (blank space, grey box, or branded fallback image).",
          "to_string": "As a Developer, \nI want a reusable pdp/gallery React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, \nso that it can be consumed by pdp/hero to render the product image and video gallery on the PDP.\n\n----\n\nThe component renders a sequence of media items (photo and video) in a stacked layout on desktop and a swipeable carousel on mobile. The desktop layout adapts based on total media count. Video is treated as a standard media item and slots into the layout based on its position in the product's media array. The component renders a View Gallery button as a trigger only — the gallery overlay is a separate component and out of scope for this story."
        }
      ],
