        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "to_string": "1. Given a shopper clicks any image in the gallery on desktop, when the image is clicked, then a full-screen overlay opens with a dark background.\n2. Given the overlay is open, when it renders, then the clicked image displays as the primary large image on the left side.\n3. Given the overlay is open, when it renders, then a vertical thumbnail strip on the right displays all gallery images as small thumbnails with the active image highlighted.\n4. Given the overlay is open, when a shopper clicks a thumbnail, then the primary image updates to display the selected image.\n5. Given the overlay is open, when a shopper scrolls the primary image panel, then they can navigate sequentially through all gallery images.\n6. Given the overlay is open, when a shopper clicks the × button or clicks outside the image area, then the overlay closes and focus returns to the PDP at the same scroll position.\n7. Given a shopper is on mobile, when they pinch on a gallery image, then pinch-to-zoom is supported within the carousel view.",
